# Nothing derived from the game may be committed. The extracted disc, the build output
# and the memory card all come from the user's own copy. `tools/check_publish.py` proves
# it before anything is published.

# The extracted disc, and any disc image in any format nodtool reads.
naruto/rom/
naruto2/rom/
*.iso
*.ciso
*.rvz
*.wia
*.gcz
*.wbfs
*.tgc
*.nfs
*.h4m
*.trk
*.bnr
*.dol

# Build output, dtk output, and the disc-derived dtk project config.
naruto/build/
naruto2/build/
config/GNREDA/
config/GNUEDA/
orig/
build/
build-*/

# The memory card and input logs. The runtime writes `saves/` beside the current
# directory, so a run started from the project root leaves one there too.
naruto/saves/
naruto2/saves/
/saves/
/inputs/

# What the launcher's device picker writes for a game: which pad each device takes on this
# machine, so it is created in the player's own copy rather than shipped.
naruto/controls.txt
naruto2/controls.txt

# Cover art the launcher shows, one file per game, named after its folder. The launcher
# fetches box art into covers/ the first time it needs it; box art belongs to the
# publisher, so it stays on the machine that has it. `git add -f` a file you drew yourself.
covers/

# A cover.png beside a game, which is where art lived before covers/ and is still read.
naruto/cover.*
naruto2/cover.*

# Local-only work trees for discs this repository does not carry, and the dtk output that
# comes from them. They stay on the machine that has them, like the disc they need.
gnt3/
gnt4/
config/G3NJDA/
config/G4NJDA/

# The launcher's build output.
launcher/build/
launcher/build-release/
launcher/dist/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.probe/probe
